What `go test -list` printed, which .github/scripts/go-test-split.test.sh feeds
.github/scripts/go-test-split.sh through GO_TEST_LIST_OUTPUT. Each file is the command's whole
standard output, captured with go1.27.3 on 2026-11-22.

logmask.txt
  cd packages/envoy && go test -list '.*' ./internal/cipher/logmask > logmask.txt
  Thirteen Tests, a Benchmark and two Fuzz targets, then the package's `ok` line.

no-test-files.txt
  go test -list '.*' ./notests > no-test-files.txt
  run in a scratch module (go.mod: `module example.com/split` and `go 1.24`) whose package
  notests holds one file, notests.go:

    package notests

    // Answer is the one declaration of a package with no test files.
    func Answer() int { return 42 }

  The package's `?` line, `[no test files]`, and no name.

test-example-fuzz.txt
  go test -list '.*' ./scratch > test-example-fuzz.txt
  run in the same scratch module, whose package scratch holds scratch.go:

    package scratch

    // Greeting is what ExampleGreeting prints.
    func Greeting() string { return "hello" }

  and scratch_test.go:

    package scratch

    import (
    	"fmt"
    	"testing"
    )

    func TestAdds(t *testing.T) {
    	if 1+1 != 2 {
    		t.Fatal("1+1 is not 2")
    	}
    }

    func ExampleGreeting() {
    	fmt.Println(Greeting())
    	// Output: hello
    }

    func FuzzReverses(f *testing.F) {
    	f.Add("seed")
    	f.Fuzz(func(t *testing.T, s string) {})
    }

  A Test, a Fuzz target and an Example, then the package's `ok` line. No package of this
  repository holds an Example, which is why this one is a scratch package.

run-pattern.txt
  go test -list '^(TestAdds|ExampleGreeting)$' ./scratch > run-pattern.txt
  run in the same scratch module: the listing go-test-split.sh reads under
  -run='^(TestAdds|ExampleGreeting)$'. The two names the pattern selects, in the order go
  prints them, without the Fuzz target, then the package's `ok` line. Captured with go1.27.3 on
  2026-11-23.

downloading.stderr.txt
  What go test -list wrote to standard error on a runner whose module cache lacked a module: the
  line go-test-split.sh, when it still read go's standard error with its output, quoted as a line
  it could not read, in job 137524299133 (`daemon-go (1/3)`) of run 45122591447, read with
  gh api --allow-escape-sequences repos/cybermonklabs/legion/actions/jobs/137524299133/logs
  (the timestamp GitHub puts before each log line taken off).
